.TH litepkg 1 "May 2, 2026" "litepkg 1.0" "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
litepkg \- A minimal and colorful AUR helper.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B litepkg
[
.B \-\-script
]
.BI COMMAND " [ARGUMENTS...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B litepkg
is a lightweight command-line utility for managing packages from the Arch User Repository (AUR). It provides a simplified interface for searching, installing, and upgrading AUR packages with colorful and compact output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B LITEPKG_CLONE_DIR
Specifies the directory where AUR repositories are cloned for building. Defaults to
.I /tmp.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-script
Enable script-friendly output. This mode uses tab-separated values and disables all ANSI color codes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI search " [OPTIONS] QUERY"
Search the AUR for packages matching the query.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-name
Search by name only.
.TP
.B \-\-maintainer
Search by maintainer name.
.TP
.B \-\-name-desc
Search by name and description.
.TP
.B \-\-description
Search in description (default).
.TP
.B \-\-popularity
Sort search results by popularity instead of name.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-orphans
Exclude packages that currently have no maintainer.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-outdated
Exclude packages marked as out-of-date in the AUR.
.RE
.TP
.BI install " PACKAGE"
Download, build, and install the specified AUR package using
.BR makepkg (8)
and
.BR pacman (8).
.TP
.BI download " PACKAGE"
Clone the AUR git repository for the specified package to the
.B LITEPKG_CLONE_DIR
without building or installing it.
.TP
.BI uninstall " PACKAGE"
Uninstall the specified package from the system using
.B pacman \-Rs.
.TP
.B list-installed
Display a list of all AUR packages currently installed on the system.
.TP
.B upgrade
Check for updates to all installed AUR packages and prompt to install them if newer versions are available.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Search for a package with popularity sorting:
.B litepkg search nodejs \-\-popularity
.TP
.B Install a specific AUR package:
.B litepkg install visual-studio-code-bin
.TP
.B Set clone directory and upgrade all AUR packages:
.B LITEPKG_CLONE_DIR=~/aur-builds litepkg upgrade
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8)
